        {
          "source_quote": "Θεῷ τῷ κτίσαντι τὸν οὐρανὸν καὶ τὸ σύμπαν οὐ λείπει πρόφασις πρὸς σωτηρίαν τῶν σώζεσθαι θελόντων.",
          "english_quote": "God, who created heaven and the universe, lacks no means for the salvation of those who wish to be saved.",
          "issue": "“Means” gives the general practical sense but obscures the framing of πρόφασις as an occasion or grounds for action, repeated later in προφάσει τῆς τοῦ σώματος θεραπείας. The note lists possible senses without explicitly comparing these linked occurrences. “Does not lack an occasion” is the more source-transparent candidate.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed for fresh review: “God, who created heaven and the universe, does not lack an occasion for the salvation of those who wish to be saved.” Explicitly document the repeated πρόφασις wording and the contextual reason for rendering its later occurrence “pretext.”",
          "severity": "minor"
        },
        {
          "source_quote": "ὅθεν μηδὲ ἐπὶ τοῖς δοκοῦσιν φαύλοις ὑπὸ προπετείας τις αὐτὸν ὡς μὴ φιλάνθρωπον αἰτιάσθω.",
          "english_quote": "Therefore, no one, through rashness, should accuse him of lacking benevolence toward humanity on account of things that appear bad.",
          "issue": "The negation is retained, but μηδὲ gives the circumstances an “even” emphasis: God should not be accused even on account of apparently bad things. That emphasis is absent.",
          "suggested_revision": "Proposed for fresh review: “Therefore, no one should rashly accuse him of lacking benevolence toward humanity, even on account of things that appear bad.”",
